{"name":"Raspberry Pudding","hex":"#94435a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raspberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Rubus idaeus.","Any of many other (but not all) species in the genus Rubus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor/flavour of raspberries.","Of a dark pinkish red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raspberry"},{"term":"pudding","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various dishes, sweet or savoury, prepared by boiling or steaming or from batter.","A type of cake or dessert cooked usually by boiling or steaming."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pudding"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raspberry","blocks":[{"text":"The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus. The name also applies to these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry","wikidata":"Q13179"},{"title":"Pudding","blocks":[{"text":"Pudding is a food which can either be a dessert or a savoury dish. In the United States, pudding means a sweet, milk-based dessert similar in consistency to egg-based custards, instant custards or a mousse, often commercially set using cornstarch, gelatin or similar coagulating agent. These puddings are known in some Commonwealth countries as custards if they are egg-thickened, as blancmange if starch-thickened, and as jelly if gelatin-based. Pudding in America may also refer to other dishes such as bread pudding and rice pudding, although typically these names derive from their origin as British dishes. The modern American meaning of pudding as dessert has evolved from the original almost exclusive use of the term to describe savoury dishes, specifically those created using a process similar to that used for sausages, in which meat and other ingredients in mostly liquid form are encased and then steamed or boiled to set the contents."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg/330px-Blanc-manger_on_glass_platter%2C_full_view.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pudding","wikidata":"Q9053"},{"title":"Raspberry (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Raspberry is a color that resembles the color of raspberries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry_(color)","wikidata":"Q3080423"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Halved_blackberry_%28Rubus_fruticosus%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHalved_blackberry_(Rubus_fruticosus)_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.j